  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quality of mechanisms in place for cooperation between CSOs and local governments</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Limited implementation of inclusive and transparent mechanisms for cooperation between civil society organizations (CSOs) and selected local governments</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Publish at least one Reload Public Call in each of 5 clusters of municipalities: Tara (Pljevlja, Kolasin and Mojkovac), Central Region (Podgorica, Golubovci, Danilovgrad and Cetinje), Together for North (Berane and Andrijevica), Together Niksic and Pluzine (Niksic and Pluzine) and Coastal Mates (Kotor, Tivat, Herceg Novi and Budva).
Allocate at least 80 % of available funds.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved capacities of 63 municipal staff and 143 NGO representatives in project cycle management, visibility and communication, gender equality, etc. Five Public Calls for NGOs launched in Clusters of municipalities: Tara, Together for North, Coastal Mtes, Central Region and Together Niksic and Pluzine, while two were re-launched in Clusters Tara and Together for North. Available grant funds for 2022 are completely utilized in Clusters Tara and Central Region, while in three Clusters utilization is from 70 - 80%. 
Under the third component Research on Local Youth Policies and Perceptions in 15 municipalities was conducted and presented to the national and local stakeholders. Further project activities on strengthening youth in local policy participation will be designed and implemented, based on Research findings and recommendations.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Close all awarded NGO Projects and spend at least 90% of available funds.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved capacities of municipal staff and NGOs and successful implementation of all contracted NGO Projects.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">MNE Local Contribution to the Regional Programme on Local Democracy in the Western Balkans 2 (ReLOaD2)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Like in the first ReLOaD phase, ReLOaD2 will focus on institutionalizing the interaction between local governments from one side and CSOs and youth from the other side , while strengthening capacities of all relevant stakeholders to engage more productively in such partnerships. Importantly, the underlying intention of the Action is to replicate and sustain a transparent, development-oriented and project-based approach to funding of CSOs by municipal budgets that contributes to realization of legitimate local priorities in line with local development strategies. Moreover, mechanisms for monitoring of projects activities and results implemented by CSOs and youth will be created and adopted, while a monitoring baseline for local government/CSO relations will be defined, introducing also appropriate tools.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
